### Plan full details — rows from COMP.V_EMPLOYEE_PLAN_FULL_DETAILS; totals from COMP.V_EMP_ASSIGNED_COMPONENTS_FULL
GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation?enterprise_id=1
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation?enterprise_id=1&employee_id=299&plan_id=80
# Pagination (defaults: page=1, limit=25; limit max 200)
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation?enterprise_id=1&page=1&limit=25
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation?enterprise_id=1&page=2&limit=25
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation?enterprise_id=1&employee_id=299&page=1&limit=10
# Regression check (allowance must NOT appear in total_base_salary):
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation?enterprise_id=1&employee_id=299&plan_id=76

### Latest component history — one row per component (ROW_NUMBER); pagination: page, limit (defaults 1 / 25; limit max 200)
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee/latest-component-history?enterprise_id=1&employee_id=299
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee/latest-component-history?enterprise_id=1&employee_id=299&plan_id=80&page=1&limit=25

### Active plan components (single employee + plan) — COMP.V_EMP_PLAN_ACTIVE_COMPONENTS_JSON
### Response adds linked salary structure (nullable): structure_id, structure_guid, structure_code, structure_name, structure_currency_code, structure_effective_from, structure_effective_to
### By id: enterprise_id, employee_id, plan_id (all required)
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee/employee-compensation-plan-details?enterprise_id=1&employee_id=1001&plan_id=200
### By guid: employee_guid + plan_guid as 32-char hex (hyphens optional); optional enterprise_id
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee/employee-compensation-plan-details?employee_guid=4CC128141B67EDF8E0633519000A56F3&plan_guid=<32_HEX_PLAN_GUID>
# GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee/employee-compensation-plan-details?enterprise_id=1&employee_guid=4CC128141B67EDF8E0633519000A56F3&plan_guid=<32_HEX_PLAN_GUID>

### Assigned components — COMP.COMP_EMP_ASSIGNED_COMPONENTS_V (employee_guid required, 32 hex; hyphens optional)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-assigned-components?employee_guid=4CC128141B67EDF8E0633519000A56F3

### Create — JSON only (no documents, no adjustment_id)
### plan_id: required on every components[] row only — do not send top-level plan_id.
### One row can use the same plan_id as another; different plan_id per row is allowed (multi-plan).
POST http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enterprise_id": 1,
  "employee_id": 1001,
  "created_by": "SYSTEM",
  "components": [
    {
      "plan_id": 80,
      "component_id": 101,
      "amount": 1000,
      "currency_code": "PKR",
      "effective_start_date": "2026-04-01",
      "effective_end_date": null,
      "active_flag": "Y"
    },
    {
      "plan_id": 81,
      "component_id": 102,
      "amount": 500,
      "currency_code": "PKR",
      "effective_start_date": "2026-04-01",
      "effective_end_date": null,
      "active_flag": "Y"
    }
  ]
}

### curl (create)
# curl -s -X POST "http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation/create" \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"enterprise_id":1,"employee_id":1001,"created_by":"SYSTEM","components":[{"plan_id":80,"component_id":101,"amount":1000,"currency_code":"PKR","effective_start_date":"2026-04-01","effective_end_date":null,"active_flag":"Y"}]}'

### Edit — multipart/form-data (adjustment + stringified components + optional BLOB documents)
### Uploaded files are NOT stored in this repo or on app disk — only persisted in Oracle (e.g. COMP_ADJUSTMENT_DOCS.FILE_CONTENT).
### enterprise_id is required (same as create). Postman form-data must include it alongside employee_id.
### plan_id: optional at top level if every components[] row includes "plan_id". Otherwise top-level plan_id is the default for rows that omit it.
### Multiple plans in one edit: send different plan_id per row (top-level plan_id may be omitted when every row has plan_id). One Oracle edit_components call → one ADJUSTMENT_ID; documents attach to that single adjustment.
### Verify (SQL as COMP): one row in COMP_ADJUSTMENT_DETAILS for the new ADJUSTMENT_ID (PLAN_ID null/absent on header); COMP_ADJUSTMENT_LINES shows one row per component with matching PLAN_ID each.
### Each object in "components" JSON must include "adjustment_method" (e.g. MANUAL, PERCENTAGE, AMOUNT_CHANGE).
### Field "components" must be valid JSON: a JSON *array* string in form-data (start with "["), e.g. [{"plan_id":80,...}] not {"plan_id":80,...}.
### Files: "documents" or "documents[]" (repeat for multiple).
### Optional: document_descriptions = JSON string array, same order as files, e.g. ["Memo","Contract"]
### Add a new pay component while updating an existing one: send multiple objects in one array, e.g.
###   [{"component_id":101,...,"adjustment_method":"MANUAL","active_flag":"Y"},{"component_id":102,...,"replace_flag":"TRUE","adjustment_method":"MANUAL","active_flag":"Y"}]
### Multi-plan components example (string in form field "components"):
# [{"plan_id":80,"component_id":101,"amount":1000,"adjustment_method":"MANUAL","currency_code":"PKR","effective_start_date":"2026-05-01","effective_end_date":null,"active_flag":"Y"},{"plan_id":81,"component_id":102,"amount":500,"adjustment_method":"MANUAL","currency_code":"PKR","effective_start_date":"2026-05-01","effective_end_date":null,"active_flag":"Y","replace_flag":"TRUE"}]
### If Oracle returns ORA-20121 / no active assignment for a component_id, that row is usually a first-time insert: set "replace_flag":"TRUE" on that object only.
### Debug: set env COMP_LOG_COMPONENT_FLAGS=1 (or true) to print a one-line components snapshot before edit_components (default off).
### Use paths to files on your machine for curl @... (do not commit sample PDFs into the project).
POST http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation/edit
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----digify

### curl (edit) — two files, components JSON inline
# COMPONENTS='[{"component_id":101,"amount":1500,"adjustment_method":"MANUAL","currency_code":"USD","effective_start_date":"2026-05-01","effective_end_date":null,"active_flag":"Y","replace_flag":"TRUE"}]'
# curl -s -X POST "http://localhost:3000/api/comp/employee-compensation/edit" \
#   -F "enterprise_id=1" \
#   -F "employee_id=1001" \
#   -F "plan_id=10" \
#   -F "adjustment_type=SALARY_INCREASE" \
#   -F "effective_date=2026-05-01" \
#   -F "reason_code=PROMOTION" \
#   -F "budget_code=HR-BUD-2026-01" \
#   -F "justification_text=Employee promoted and salary revised." \
#   -F "performance_rating=EXCEEDS_EXPECTATIONS" \
#   -F "internal_notes=Reviewed by HR and line manager." \
#   -F "updated_by=SYSTEM" \
#   -F "components=${COMPONENTS}" \
#   -F "document_descriptions=[\"Offer letter\",\"Signed addendum\"]" \
#   -F "documents=@/path/to/file1.pdf" \
#   -F "documents=@/path/to/file2.pdf"
